<title>DENMARK: Danish June trade surplus 2.734 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish June trade surplus 2.734 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 2.734 billion crowns in June 1996 compared to a revised 3.554 billion crowns in May 1996, the national statistics office said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     June 1996    May 1996  June 1995</p>
<p> Exports			23.403	24.516     24.260</p>
<p> Imports			20.416	20.667     20.991</p>
<p> Trade balance		 2.987	 3.848	3.270</p>
<p> Trade balance excl ships  2.734	 3.554	3.177</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted</p>
<p> balance excluding ships   1.282	 4.094	2.473</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters on average forecast a June surplus excluding ships of 3.8 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
